<title>HONG KONG: HK stamps with Queen's head not valid from July 1.</title>
<headline>HK stamps with Queen's head not valid from July 1.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong stamps with the portrait of Britain's Queen Elizabeth will cease to be valid when the territory reverts to China on July 1, the government said on Monday.</p>
<p>People can exchange the stamps for new ones of the same value between July 3 and July 31, it said. The new stamps bear an image of the Victoria Harbour skyline.</p>
<p>But many people are expected to keep the old stamps as relics of a bygone era, or for their potential collectors' value. At midnight on June 30, Britain will hand the colony of more than 150 years back to China.</p>
</text>
